{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3140","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3140","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3140\",\"parent_revision\":\"693d5d57a3fad3d0af8361030cd5e797bff3ec7b74a5aa23d013fcf3eb13a62f\",\"root_revision\":\"693d5d57a3fad3d0af8361030cd5e797bff3ec7b74a5aa23d013fcf3eb13a62f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGoal: close the path that produced the #3060 over-orchestration incident, where a task-level agent was handed a plan-level skill to run and recursively re-entered the workflow its own dispatcher was already running.\\n\\nRoot cause established by forensic analysis: the dispatcher hand-composed a free-prose delegation prompt that named a plan-management skill. Nothing in the system produced that prompt, so nothing constrained it. The skill name reached a task-level agent purely because a human-readable string was assembled by hand.\\n\\nEvery receiver-side remedy has now been tried and rejected. Prose in the dispatched agent's own file cannot carry the constraint, because a dispatched agent cannot observe which workflow level dispatched it \u2014 the one fact the constraint depends on. Prose telling the dispatcher to be careful is ignorable by construction.\\n\\nThe remaining option is to remove hand-composition: have the delegation prompt for a ready task be returned by a tool, so the dispatcher passes through a generated prompt rather than writing one. The prompt's content is then determined by the task record and the plan's own state, which are the things that actually know what level the work sits at.\\n\\nImpact: affects every dispatch path in the development-harness plugin. Reduces a class of failure that currently recurs and is only caught after the fact.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a SAM action returning the delegation prompt for a ready task is the shape suggested during analysis; it has not been scoped and the code change to sam_schema is unestimated. Forensic report: .tmp/scratch/reports/20260821-task-worker-over-orchestration.md\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **delegation prompts for sam tasks should be produced by a tool, not hand-composed** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Root cause of the #3060 over-orchestration incident\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"82fced6af003db6c37680c27c8ec5780542e5d8e379f8b53071602698bc8cc5b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQLLi9A\"}"}